<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 29.45 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 29.45 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	29.45	    + 11	    28.84     29.95</p>
<p>91-Day	28.90	    -120	    28.39     29.27</p>
<p>182-Day     27.69	    -161	    27.31     27.90</p>
<p>364-Day     27.15				27.00     27.29</p>
<p>Last week 336-day paper was assigned at 28.63 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.23 bln pesos     2.48</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   2.77 bln pesos     3.08</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   3.39 bln pesos     3.77</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   3.11 bln pesos     5.18</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.48 compared with 3.03 the week before, on demand of 10.01 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			 50   basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			 37   basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			21   basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			14   basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
